<description>&lt;p&gt;Police recruitment in South Sudan has sparked fears of a clampdown ahead of the first elections, while President Kiir has reshuffled the Jonglei state government. In Kajo-Keji County, 20 civilians were killed, and a separate ambush on the Juba-Nimule road left seven dead. Traders at Gudele market report rising prices as customers disappear, and Western Equatoria has stepped up Ebola prevention measures. A dispute over oversight of the Oil Revenue Committee has emerged in Ulang County, and the UN envoy has urged South Sudanese leaders to choose consensus over confrontation. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikgFBVV95cUxPdWV5SWFKTzZlbFNPdXQzUUNvTmNmTUJVQVBfcmdRYWlRSkNYREU3ZzN3WldwQ0F0bndRc1BkQlpNN2VVdE9CUnR0U29iYlpQUGVYZ1hlc0pBaDJ5SlR0aHcyam5JVjN3bUItN0F6YVpXdEswWWZLV1BJWjZfNVo0M1lVM0xiYnMyaDFVUzlZT1hnUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxQZEVtdGNReTFodzlycGNnLW5hSVh3SUdWMlJ0RUlhQ0hGdUR2U2NuUTZyanA1aVlhY1RDX0RkSzB4ZjY0dlR1elJXWGZGZ0lrWEszVGNNTjMydklVZkRSUHprZFBlM1dPYkRSMENhNGtrR0JwSnZvRmlCQVNWUWY2dUZWeTlqaUlsRGhvZzhEOEwySW1aSlFWNFZCcGRBNEtURUtPMi1ZY0RQU2hTUFV0aGp3?oc=5&quot;&gt;Ahram Online&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxQdDFvN0tkT2oxM0Rzc25IQkh2WmgzVVNVN2dwSkZYa0FMeHJTUVVRd0R3Nkl2U1dDOGhxX1duS1l2ZWVuUkFBYVQ1MmV6UFhEWWMzd1JvMW5NWG52cHcyV2lLbm5iMlMyQ0k2Sk9URHZMMTlORmRielNmRFZuNDFiQ2hwLXlBamk1aDNZZG1B?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sudans Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxQRElreEtiQW5JekdnM0pja3JvMW9kWXNGX0lLcUdwRTlkQll0SDJkVGVlRzNxZ3Y2NGoweWNMY3VGQkdpU2x1Q2tyLWd2a1ZLbHRvTmJBYnQtdGRsQmt1QU5vRlZQNFhjb054ZXpOR3BoQ1NNS1NnOGFzcWZnTWEyVFFET3Zud1dZQUdNTTRn?oc=5&quot;&gt;Oxfam&lt;/a&